{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1195479-thallain-and-unseelie-court","id":1195479,"title":"Thallain and Unseelie court","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-14T14:46:08-07:00","id":1195479,"title":"Thallain and Unseelie court","content":"So, I'm reading a great novel of the Dreaming called the Toybox (<a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Toybox-Immortal-Eyes-Trilogy-Book/dp/1565048601\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.amazon.com/Toybox-Immort.../dp/1565048601</a>) and in it it mention the equivalent of Seelie Troll being Unseelie Ogre. According to C20, Ogres aren't Kithain but Thallain. Is this a novelist mistake ? Can Thallain be part of the Unseelie court ? The book says they can never be Seelie, but only mention they could join the Shadow Court.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13714-ventrue-pimp","name":"Ventrue Pimp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T14:54:29-07:00","id":1195480,"title":"","content":"Ogre is also a term for an unseelie troll, just like goblin is a term for an unseelie nocker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T15:34:31-07:00","id":1195504,"title":"","content":"You\u2019ll find discrepancies in just about all the Changeling fiction. They\u2019re either a product of artistic license to tell a better story or they\u2019re an artifact from being written before some of Changeling\u2019s details were really set. Also, some things like Thallain mechanics changed between editions. In first and second edition, Thallain had two unseelie legacies. In C20, they get a nightmare legacy. I wouldn\u2019t sweat the details. Just enjoy the stories on their own terms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}